# Server-side Postgres (Phase 1 — docker-compose.yml's "postgres" service).
# Only set on the server's .env, never locally. Docker compose reads these
# from .env directly for the service's ${...} substitution, and passes them
# to "app" and "directus" as discrete connection fields (see PGHOST/etc and
# docs/DIRECTUS.md below).
POSTGRES_DB=
POSTGRES_USER=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Server-side Directus (Phase 2 — docker-compose.yml's "directus" service).
# Only set on the server's .env. Reuses POSTGRES_DB/USER/PASSWORD above to
# connect — see docs/DIRECTUS.md for why, and the TODO to split it out later.
# KEY/SECRET are Directus's own encryption/signing keys, generated fresh for
# this environment (openssl rand -hex 32) — never copied from a local .env.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD: served over HTTPS at admin.woodclay.ru since 2026-08-10 —
# the value here only matters for a fresh install/bootstrap. To change the
# live login, use the Directus CLI (see docs/DIRECTUS.md), not this file.
DIRECTUS_KEY=
DIRECTUS_SECRET=
DIRECTUS_ADMIN_EMAIL=
DIRECTUS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Selectel S3-compatible object storage — the bucket product photos live in.
# Same credentials the (separate) seed project uses to upload WB images, and
# now also read by the "directus" service for the own-image-upload extension
# (drag-and-drop into own_images — see directus-admin/extensions). Only set
# on the server's .env; get these from the Selectel control panel.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_SECRET_KEY=
S3_REGION=
S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Wildberries API keys, one set per store account (wb_account 1|2|3 — see
# db/schema.ts). 1/2 are copies (not moves) of the same keys catalog-seed/.env
# uses; 3 is a store with no catalog-seed presence at all — this repo is its
# only consumer. CONTENT is the "Контент" category (content-api.wildberries.ru
# — scripts/backfill-wb-dimensions.mjs, scripts/import-new-wb-products.mjs).
# PRICES covers both discounts-prices-api and marketplace-api (same key
# scope, see catalog-seed's wbPrices.ts/wbStock.ts) — only import-new-wb-products
# needs it, to price/stock a brand-new product. Get/rotate from the WB seller
# cabinet.
WB_CONTENT_KEY_1=
WB_CONTENT_KEY_2=
WB_CONTENT_KEY_3=
WB_PRICES_KEY_1=
WB_PRICES_KEY_2=
WB_PRICES_KEY_3=

# Catalogue database (Phase 3 — db/client.ts). Required; the app throws at
# startup if any of these is unset. Discrete fields, not a single connection
# string — POSTGRES_PASSWORD can contain characters that aren't safe
# unescaped inside a URL, so this sidesteps ever needing to encode it.
# - Locally: point at an SSH tunnel to the server Postgres (see
#   docs/RESTORE.md for the tunnel pattern), e.g. PGHOST=localhost,
#   PGPORT=5433, PGUSER=woodclay_app, PGDATABASE=woodclay.
# - On the server: NOT set here directly — docker-compose.yml's "app"
#   service sets these inline from POSTGRES_DB/USER/PASSWORD above, the same
#   way the "directus" service does.
PGHOST=
PGPORT=
PGDATABASE=
PGUSER=
PGPASSWORD=

# Local-only, optional. Used by drizzle-kit (drizzle.config.ts) for
# `db:generate`/`studio`/`migrate` — a single connection-string URL, since
# that's what drizzle-kit's own config expects (unrelated to the app's own
# PGHOST/etc above). Point it at the same SSH tunnel, e.g.
# postgres://woodclay_app:<password>@localhost:5433/woodclay — if the
# password needs URL-encoding for this one, encode it here by hand.
DATABASE_URL=

# Accounts (Phase 4 — auth.ts). AUTH_SECRET signs/encrypts the session JWT —
# generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`, same as DIRECTUS_KEY/SECRET above.
# COOKIE_SECURE must stay "false" while the site is served over plain HTTP
# (the browser silently drops a Secure-flagged cookie on non-HTTPS origins,
# which would break login entirely) — flip to "true" the moment HTTPS lands.
# See docs/DIRECTUS.md's Security TODOs.
AUTH_SECRET=
COOKIE_SECURE=false

# SMTP for email verification codes (lib/mailer.ts). The mailbox
# woodandclay.help@mail.ru is already the support address linked in the
# account page footer — SMTP_USER doubles as the From address (mail.ru
# rejects a mismatched From). Needs an app password, not the account's login
# password: mail.ru → Настройки → Пароль и безопасность → Пароли для
# внешних приложений.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.mail.ru
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# ЮKassa payment (Phase 6 — lib/yookassa.ts). These are a *test shop*'s
# credentials from the ЮKassa dashboard (sandbox) — there is no separate
# sandbox API host, so going live later is only ever swapping these two
# values for the live shop's real ones, nothing else changes. Get them from
# https://yookassa.ru/my (Настройки → тестовый магазин).
YUKASSA_SHOP_ID=
YUKASSA_SECRET_KEY=

# СДЭК pickup-point picker (Phase 7 — app/(shop)/catalog/cart/CdekPvzPicker.tsx,
# app/api/cdek/offices, app/api/dadata/suggest-cities, lib/shipping.ts).
# Hand-built picker: DaData for fuzzy city search + a real Yandex map for
# pins (coordinates come from CDEK's own /deliverypoints, no geocoding
# needed for that part) — see the note in CdekPvzPicker.tsx for why this
# isn't CDEK's own @cdek-it/widget (that needs a *separately paid* Yandex
# HTTP Geocoder license as of the May 2026 Yandex product split; the plain
# JS API used here for map display only is still free).
# CDEK_CLIENT_ID/SECRET: OAuth2 client-credentials for СДЭК API v2, from
# "Интеграция" → "Создать ключ" in the СДЭК личный кабинет — works even
# before a full business contract is approved (test-account limitations
# apply: test orders aren't fulfilled). Swap for live values once the
# contract is approved.
CDEK_CLIENT_ID=
CDEK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Yandex Maps JS API key, exposed to the browser (the map renders
# client-side). Generate at yandex.ru/dev/maps ("JavaScript API" product
# only — do NOT pay for/attach the HTTP Geocoder, we don't call it). Free
# under standard conditions (public page, don't strip the Yandex logo,
# stay under the daily request cap). We only ever place markers from known
# coordinates (ymaps.Placemark) — never call ymaps.geocode() or a Suggest
# control, since those route through the paid Geocoder product and will
# 403 with "Invalid api key" even though the map itself loads fine.
# On the server: also needs to be set here even though this var otherwise
# only matters at `next build` time (NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the
# client bundle, not read at runtime) — docker-compose.yml's app.build.args
# reads it from this file via ${...} substitution and forwards it into the
# image build as a Docker build arg, since .dockerignore excludes .env
# itself from the build context. Rebuild the image after changing it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YANDEX_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Яндекс.Метрика counter id (analytics/, ConsentBanner + YandexMetrika
# components). Same NEXT_PUBLIC_* build-time-only rule as the Maps key
# above — inlined into the client bundle at `next build`, so it needs the
# same docker-compose.yml app.build.args wiring, and a rebuild after
# changing it. Metrika only ever initializes client-side after the visitor
# accepts the cookie-consent banner, so this being public is fine — it's
# just a counter id, not a secret. Create the counter at metrika.yandex.ru.
NEXT_PUBLIC_YANDEX_METRIKA_ID=
# DaData suggest API — fuzzy Russian city search (CDEK's own /location/cities
# is exact-match only). Server-side only, never exposed to the browser (see
# app/api/dadata/suggest-cities). Free up to 10,000 requests/day. Get a
# token at dadata.ru → sign up, confirm email → Кабинет → API-ключи.
DADATA_API_KEY=
# Flat СДЭК ПВЗ-to-ПВЗ shipping rate in rubles — provisional, see
# lib/shipping.ts. One place to change it: edit here, restart the app
# container, no rebuild needed.
SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE_RUB=450

# Telegram bot used to deliver corporate-quote form submissions
# (app/api/corporate-quote/route.ts). Both required for the form to work.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Optional. HTTP proxy URL (e.g. http://xray:1080) for the outbound
# Telegram API call only — needed when api.telegram.org isn't directly
# reachable from the server's network (see docker-compose.yml's xray
# service). Leave unset if the server can reach Telegram directly.
TELEGRAM_PROXY_URL=
